  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Solafuranone may interact with the CD276 antigen through a series of molecular pathways. The drug is linked to Caspase-2, which is a target of multiple compounds, including 2,8-Dimethoxy-3-Methylnaphthalen-1-Ol and [(1S,4R,4aS,7S,8R,8aR)-8-[2-(furan-3-yl)ethyl]-1,7-dihydroxy-7,8-dimethyl-5-oxospiro[2,3,6,8a-tetrahydro-1H-naphthalene-4,2'-oxirane]-4a-yl]methyl acetate. These compounds, in turn, target the CD276 antigen, indicating a potential mechanism by which Solafuranone may influence the CD276 antigen. The scores for these relationships are consistent, suggesting a plausible biological link. The evidence supports a possible role for Solafuranone in modulating the CD276 antigen through the Caspase-2 pathway, though the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated.",
